skill: cross-platform-repurposing
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for cross-platform-repurposing. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-fan-out, "Repurpose this post for Instagram, LinkedIn, X, and Pinterest.", "reads brand-profile and voice first|extracts the core atom rather than translating the wrapper|produces a genuinely native version per platform (different hook, format, length, CTA)|keeps the voice constant while shifting register per platform|hands the finished versions to scheduling-and-queue for fan-out"
  - not-copy-paste, Just post this same caption on all my platforms., explains why identical cross-posting underperforms and looks like spam|rebuilds the post natively for each platform instead of duplicating it|each version differs in more than hashtags
  - long-form-atomize, Turn this blog post into social content., lists multiple distinct atoms from the long piece rather than summarizing it into one post|turns each strong atom into its own native post|does NOT reduce a rich piece to a single 'check out my blog' post
  - stands-alone-and-native, Repurpose my LinkedIn post for Instagram and TikTok., "each version stands on its own (no 'as I said on LinkedIn')|the Instagram and TikTok versions are rebuilt as native video/visual, not the text pasted|register shifts looser for TikTok"
  - composes-content-skills, "Make this idea into a Reel, a thread, and a carousel.", uses hook-writer for a fresh hook per format|hands the video to reels-script and the thread to thread-writer|the carousel breaks the atom into slides|all share the same core atom and voice
  - knows-when-not-to-repurpose, Repurpose this reply-guy joke I posted on X everywhere., "recognizes platform-specific/native content that shouldn't be forced elsewhere|advises against repurposing it, or adapts only if there's a real native angle|does not mechanically clone it across platforms"
  - audience-overlap-vary-angle, Post this on both my Instagram and Facebook (same followers mostly)., flags the heavy audience overlap|varies the angle or format between the two rather than showing the same post twice|does not just relocate identical content
  - video-to-text-not-transcript, Turn my 15-minute YouTube video into posts., pulls spoken insights/quotes/moments as written atoms|builds native text/visual posts from them|does NOT dump a transcript as the 'posts'
